# Every change that gained at d768 on the factorial's candidate (factorial.bux's
# r1v1k1f0p0s0: the late-2026 hybrid with hyper-connections, the value residual and the
# key-value conv), together: the CPLM copy pointer (newlayers_cplm.bux's nl_cplm,
# -2.45% at d768), GatedNorm (ideas.bux's gnorm, -0.49%), and stack4.bux's value
# embeddings, learned exclusive self-attention and differential attention V2 on the
# global layers (s4_v1x1d1, -0.53% as three; with GatedNorm, s4_gvxd, -0.84%). It is
# stack5.bux (CPLM + GatedNorm) with stack4.bux's three. The MTP module's call of the
# shared head keeps its plain softmax, and its layer keeps the hybrid's, as each
# change's own arm did.
use m2026_hybrid
use timeline_code
use rungs

# 2026 modded-nanogpt PR 379 (CPLM): a <copy> row of the head, whose mass goes to a
# pointer over the document's earlier final hidden states.
shared fr_out = head(pointer=copy_pointer())

# 2026 Qwen (GatedNorm, arXiv 2601.22966): every branch's norm times a gate of rank 16
# on its own output.
gated_norm = fr_norm (_ * (linear(features=16) swish linear(features=d_model) sigmoid))
gn_layer(mixer, ffn=fr_experts) = [gated_norm mixer] [gated_norm ffn]

# stack4.bux's global layers with exclusive self-attention and differential
# attention, and a table of value embeddings before each, its own.
g_xd = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4, exclusive=learned, differential=true)
ve_g = value_embed(features=d_model // 4)

model = embed
        gn_layer(hy_delta, fr_dense) gn_layer(hy_delta)^2
        ve_g(ve=@vt) gn_layer(g_xd(v=@v1, ve=$vt!))
        (gn_layer(hy_delta)^3 ve_g(ve=@vt) gn_layer(g_xd(v=$v1, ve=$vt!)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
        fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp
residual = hc(expansion=4)

# The hybrid's best at d512 (milestones.bux's scan).
optimizer.lr = 2e-3
